<!--
    Objective-C message sends typed and resolved by their receiver
    (`option objcrettype on|off`, `option objcresolve on|off`).

    Issue: a message send names its selector but not its method, and the
    runtime entry points are typed once for every receiver. `-[Holder make]` of
    the ARC fixture printed `objc_object *v1 = objc_alloc_init(_OBJC_CLASS_$_Base);
    objc_msgSend(v1,sel_setInner_,objc_alloc_init(...));` - the alloc/init
    result an `id`, the send an opaque runtime call although `-[Base setInner:]`
    is a method of the image. `-[Holder innerCount]` of the types fixture sent
    `objc_msgSend(self->inner,sel_count)` to an ivar typed `Base *` and
    `objc_msgSend$inner(self)` to a `Holder *`.

    Fix: the ObjC analysis hands the engine its class table (own methods,
    superclass, class_t and selector addresses; `p5_types/kuna_objcrettype.rs`).
    P5 `TypeOpCall::getOutputLocal` answers for `alloc`/`new`/`objc_alloc*` on a
    folded class reference with that class's pointer and for `init.../self/
    retain/autorelease/copy` with the receiver's class (`objcrettype`); the P9
    callee name of a send whose receiver's class is known is the method it
    reaches, looked up along the superclass chain, and a second decompile
    sends the CALL to that IMP (`FlowInfo::setup_call_specs` retarget), so
    the call carries the method's prototype and `kuna xrefs` its edge
    (`objcresolve`).

    Pass 1 (both off): `objc_object *v1`, `objc_msgSend(v1,sel_setInner_,...)`,
    `objc_msgSend(self->inner,sel_count)`. Pass 2 (default): `Base *v1`,
    `-[Base setInner:](v1,...)`, `-[Base count](self->inner,sel_count)`,
    `-[Holder inner](...)`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
